WEBVTT

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.760
What?

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.550
It's already sold out?  Why?

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.280
It is what it is.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.240
The new extra sweet red bean 
noodle soup are very popular.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.240
Anyway, stop making us come with 
you to buy something so stupid!

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.110
Do you know how hard I worked to find 
out that this store was selling it?

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.350
You should do real work instead!

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.960
You can always come back and buy it again.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:45.750
It's mine!

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.490
A thief!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.000
What?

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.240
What happened?

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:01.230
They're mine.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:08.590
You risked your life to retrieve 
this old granny's cup ramen.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:12.200
You're a saint!

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.360
No, I…

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.990
Take one as a reward.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.820
In that case...

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.860
I accept!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.560
I know that annoying laugh.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.630
Yeager.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.710
Why is he here?

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.350
Riding Duels.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.420
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:43.240
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:04.540
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:14.650
Soar in the infinite skies  BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.890
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.860
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:32.630
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:38.240
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:44.610
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:50.420
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:56.720
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:03.030
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:32.860
Project Capture Yeager II!

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.800
I haven't had a feast in a long time, but 
it'll be the new extra sweet red bean noodle soup!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.340
You seem pretty happy, Yeager.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.930
Long time, no see.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.240
You're mistaking me for someone else.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:51.930
Stop fooling around!

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.610
We're not making a mistake!

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:57.880
No matter how you dress…

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.360
With your weird voice...

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.330
That's proof!

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.760
Oh no!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.660
I want to ask you something.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.980
What?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:14.700
Since you're Vice Director of the Public 
Maintenance Department, you must know about Iliaster.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.090
You want me to tell you about Iliaster?

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.100
What do I get in return?

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:26.330
Don't get cocky!  You stole my cup ramen!

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.150
Don't say that you forgot!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.480
Talk!  Now!

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.050
Calm down, Jack.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.270
You can't understand my frustration!

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:41.880
What?

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:52.340
Your cup ramen was delicious!  Bye!

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.810
He's always quick to escape!

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.550
Even though there were four of 
you, he still escaped easily?

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:04.480
Why?

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.520
Why?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.790
Someone started talking 
about cup ramen and revenge.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.220
Are you saying that it was my fault?

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.290
Maybe.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.190
But why was Yeager there?

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:19.120
Iliaster is also after him.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.500
Since he's in danger, he acts 
like he doesn't know anything.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.750
He must have information about Iliaster.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.670
Want to try to catch him again?

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.210
I don't think we can find him easily.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.140
Yeah.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.110
That punk.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.100
I have a good idea!

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.910
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.530
It's been a long time since we had a feast!

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.070
Where did you get this, dear?

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:01.020
Atsuko, that's not something 
you need to worry about.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.130
It looks delicious!

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.710
Kaoru, eat up.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.150
Father, you're not going to eat?

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:17.320
I already ate, so I'm fine.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.920
Thank you for this meal!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.270
Dear…

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.440
Maybe I'll have the soup.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.840
Today is Spicy Red Dragon Archfiend Noodles!

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.650
Thanks for coming to commemorate the 3rd 
anniversary since the product's launch!

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:44.870
Today's special guest is Cup Ramen Man!

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.190
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:52.520
What is that?

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.880
Lame.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.760
Why do I have to dress up like this?

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.330
Because you lost in rock-paper-scissors.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.130
Jack, you punk!  I won't forget this!

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.010
What is Crow muttering about?

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:09.960
Who knows.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:16.700
Let's begin the Spicy Red Dragon 
Archfiend Noodles Duel Tournament!

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.420
You'll battle against the 
mighty duelist Cup Ramen Man!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:25.820
If you win, you get a year's worth of 
Spicy Red Dragon Archfiend Noodles!

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.760
A year's worth?  That's generous!

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.930
Even I think I can win!

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:29.930
I don't feel like losing!

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.020
I'll battle!

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.770
What?

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.160
Duel!

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:36.790
My turn!

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.060
I attack you directly!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.660
Come back another time!

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:41.670
I lost!

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.390
This will finish you!

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.040
Wow!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.370
He's on a different level!

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.850
Who's next?

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.740
I shall be the next opponent.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.110
Oops.  I mean to say that 
it's gonna be me!  Yeah!

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.630
He's here!

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.560
I'm happy to meet you again!

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.400
Have I seen you before?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.410
We won't let you escape this time!

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.700
We were waiting for you!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.910
Give up!

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.370
How annoying!  However…

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:24.950
What's this?

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.060
Farewell!

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.820
What's going on?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.530
Yeager, you punk!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.930
Where did he go?

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:39.030
He escaped again.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:41.210
It's fine.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.550
I was ready this time.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.310
I can't let those fools catch me!

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:55.870
Those fools?

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.880
Are you talking about us?

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.160
You're giving us a hard time.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:11.280
How did you know I was here?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:16.030
We can't let you continue to escape, 
so we put a transmitter on you.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.770
I'll now get my revenge for the cup ramen!

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.500
Can you tell us about Iliaster?

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.610
I have nothing to tell you!

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.500
Then how's this for an idea?

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.950
We never finished our 
duel.  Let's end it now!

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.220
What?

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:40.410
If you win, we'll stop chasing you.  If 
I win, you'll tell us about Iliaster.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:48.150
Fine!  I'll show you my skills!

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.660
Good!

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.560
Duel!

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:04.780
I go first!

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:05.480
Bring it!

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.070
My turn!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.600
First, I set four cards.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.790
He set four cards at once?

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:15.500
Then I summon Jester Lord.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.860
That's the same monster as last time.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:25.640
When there are no other 
monsters on the field,

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:29.270
Jester Lord's attack points are 
equal to the number of cards

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.280
in our Spell & Trap Card 
Zones multiplied by 1000.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:38.820
He instantly increased its attack 
points to 4000.  He's tricky as usual!

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:46.080
Don't underestimate the skills of the Public 
Maintenance Department's Vice Director!  I end my turn!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:50.700
A bluff from a clown won't fool me!  My turn!

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:53.530
Since a monster is on 
your field, I can summon

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:57.300
Blackwing – Sirocco the Dawn 
without releasing another monster!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:06.000
And Jester Lord's attack points return to 0!

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:10.210
Then I activate Imperial Register.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.120
When one monster's attack points decrease,

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:18.660
I can add the same number of points to one of 
my monster's attack points until the End Phase!

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:23.140
Therefore, Jester Lord's 
attack points return to 4000!

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:31.670
In that case, I Special Summon 
Blackwing – Gale the Whirlwind!

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:39.370
I can Special Summon this card 
when a Blackwing is on my field!

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:44.280
That's a Tuner Monster.  You're 
planning to Synchro Summon.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:48.350
In that case, I activate the 
Continuous Trap Discord!

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:56.460
Both players can't Synchro 
Summon for three turns!

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:01.460
You're preventing Synchros again?  You 
shouldn't underestimate my Blackwings!

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:04.380
I activate Gale the Whirlwind's effect!

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:10.840
Once a turn, Gale the Whirlwind can halve 
one of your monsters' attack and defense points!

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:15.810
Furthermore, Sirocco the Dawn 
can give its attack points

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.060
to a Blackwing on my field once a turn!

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:21.980
How's that?

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:29.820
You fell for my trap!  I activate 
the Continuous Trap Tuning Barrier!

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:33.360
If a player has a Tuner Monster on his field

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:36.930
or in his graveyard, he can't 
attack for three turns!

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:40.480
This is bad!  Gale the 
Whirlwind is a Tuner Monster!

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:44.160
Yeager further strengthened his defense.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.940
But it looks like Crow has a plan.

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:47.910
What?

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:50.650
Yeah, I do.  This is my plan!

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.260
I remove Gale the Whirlwind 
and Sirocco the Dawn from play

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:58.140
to Special Summon Blackwing – 
Aurora the Northern Lights!

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:08.000
I can Special Summon it by removing a 
Blackwing Tuner and a non-Tuner monster from play.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:13.700
This card's Level is equal to the total 
Level of the monsters that were removed from play!

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:17.410
Once a turn, I can remove 
a Blackwing Synchro Monster

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.810
in my Extra Deck with the 
same Level from play...

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:25.280
...and it gains that monster's attack 
points and effects until my next turn!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.540
Aurora the Northern Lights is Level 8!

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.820
I remove Level 8 Blackwing – 
Silverwind the Ascendant from play!

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:42.290
Aurora the Northern Lights 
has 2800 attack points?

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.630
That's right!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.970
Not only did it gain attack points, but since

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:50.220
Aurora the Northern Lights isn't a Synchro 
Monster, Discord doesn't affect it!

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:55.180
And since the Tuner was removed from play, 
Tuning Barrier doesn't affect it either.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:58.880
Even though his Synchros are sealed away, 
he can still battle using this strategy.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.130
Good thinking, Crow.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:08.860
After our previous duel, I thought about ways to 
counter an Anti Synchro deck.  This is the result!

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:13.800
Battle!  Aurora the Northern 
Lights attacks Jester Lord!

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:17.940
I send Blackwing – Kalut the 
Moon Shadow to the graveyard

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:22.710
to give its attack points to 
Aurora the Northern Lights!

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.030
What?

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.550
I set a card and end my turn!

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.640
No way!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.770
How's that, punk?

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.150
Ouch!  Who did that?

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.400
Stop bullying my father!

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.400
You two!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.770
So you're the one who's 
always bullying my father!

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.300
I'm not a bully!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.570
Anyway, you have a family?

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.370
Of course!  Even though I look like 
this, I'm a fine member of society!

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:59.830
A fine member of society?  
Don't make me laugh!

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.110
This place is dangerous.  Stay back!

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:03.850
Dear…

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:07.330
Father, beat up those bad guys!

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:10.180
We're not bad guys!

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:14.360
Don't worry.  Justice always wins.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.660
You steal other people's cup 
ramen!  You're not justice!

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:22.170
Be quiet!  Let's continue the duel!  My turn!

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.410
I activate the Continuous 
Trap Imperial Custom!

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.450
Then I summon Jester Queen!

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:36.200
When this card is successfully summoned,

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:40.220
all spell and trap cards on my 
field are supposed to be destroyed.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:47.080
However, since Imperial Custom is active, all 
non-Imperial Custom Continuous Traps aren't destroyed.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:52.260
He went through all that trouble for 
a monster with only 800 attack points?

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:57.650
Don't insult my father!  My 
father is planning something!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.340
Next, I activate the Continuous 
Spell Hidden Passage!

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:10.110
When my monsters have fewer attack points than your 
monsters, one of my monsters can attack you directly!

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.600
In other words, it's a direct 
attack with 800 attack points.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:20.300
No.  Jester Queen can attack for every 
spell and trap card on my field!

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:26.960
Since Yeager has four cards on his 
field, he can attack four times!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.430
What?

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:32.800
Jester Queen, attack him four times directly!

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:52.620
Crow!

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:53.360
This is bad!

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:55.830
Wow!

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.060
Dear!

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:04.000
I can't let you or Iliaster capture me!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.410
But if you keep running, nothing will change!

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:11.370
Can't you understand that?  Let's 
battle against Iliaster together!

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:15.150
My turn!

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:18.370
Aurora the Northern Lights's effect vanishes.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:24.760
I can Special Summon this card 
when a Blackwing is on my field.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:28.220
I Special Summon Blackwing 
– Bora the Spear!

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:32.320
I release two Blackwings!

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:37.930
I Tribute Summon Blackwing 
– Abrolhos the Megaquake!

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.670
2600 attack points...

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:43.540
All right!  Attack and finish him, Crow!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.410
Dear!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:47.110
It's okay!  Father won't lose!

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:49.230
Father, do your best!

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:54.050
Even if I had to run away from 
Iliaster for the rest of my life,

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:58.370
I will protect my family!  
I can't afford to lose!

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.790
Protect your family?

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.420
Father, you're cool!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.860
He has 1800 life points remaining.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:10.170
I activate Abrolhos the Megaquake's effect!

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:13.340
It loses 1000 attack points 
until the End Phase,

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:17.780
and all cards in your Spell & Trap 
Card Zone return to your hand!

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:19.410
Why?

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:22.880
Abrolhos the Megaquake, attack Jester Queen!

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:32.970
The card that battled against 
my monster isn't destroyed,

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:35.760
and it returns to your hand 
after damage calculation!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.000
What is that idiot doing?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:42.400
If Crow attacked without using its effect, 
he could've dropped his life points to 0.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.200
Crow…

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:47.510
I can't believe I miscalculated 
the damage.  I'm losing my touch.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:48.740
I end my turn!

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:50.980
Win!

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:52.740
Father, win!

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:53.810
Dear!

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:55.980
My turn!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.950
Go, Father!

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:00.160
I summon Jester Queen!

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:07.460
Next, I activate Jester's Panic from my hand!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.030
I look at one of your set cards.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:16.090
By sending the same type of card to the 
graveyard, the card I look at is destroyed!

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:24.840
When that destruction is successful, one 
Jester monster on my field can attack you directly!

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:27.590
Now show me your set card!

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:33.120
Hooray!  Father is going to win!

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:37.020
This is bad.  Blackwing - Boobytrap 
deals 1000 points of damage

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:39.520
to the opponent when it's destroyed.

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:44.300
Since Yeager now knows what his set card 
is, he won't destroy Blackwing - Boobytrap.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:51.400
If I activate Hidden Passage and attack 
him directly with Jester Queen, I win.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:57.340
But what should've happened 
on the last turn was...

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:01.610
I can't believe I miscalculated 
the damage.  I'm losing my touch.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:04.910
Crow is trying to lose on purpose.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.920
For my son who believes in me…

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:13.190
...I can't afford to lose!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.430
Bring it!

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.290
It's all over!

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.760
Father!

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:20.970
Due to the effect of Jester's 
Panic, I send a trap card

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:24.040
to the graveyard to destroy 
Blackwing - Boobytrap!

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:31.380
You idiot!  Blackwing - 
Boobytrap's effect activates!

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:36.480
When this card is destroyed, 
you take 1000 points of damage!

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:53.830
No way…  My father can't lose!

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:56.390
Yeager, why?

00:20:57.470 --> 00:21:00.900
I can't afford to lose.

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:04.980
I can't protect my family 
if I lose to Iliaster!

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:07.160
Yeager…

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:09.550
Kaoru…

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:11.720
There's no need to cry.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:14.760
I lost in order to fight.

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.160
So that I can protect you!

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:19.590
Dear!

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:21.190
My family!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:27.100
He wasted my kindness.  
He's so uncooperative.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:29.930
I can say the same about you, Crow.

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:38.500
As promised, I'll tell you everything I know

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:43.010
about the Public Maintenance 
Department and Iliaster!

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:56.430
Close to you  Keep what's 
precious in your heart

00:21:56.890 --> 00:22:03.130
There's only one shining 
soul that's next to you

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:21.420
You always pretend and hide your fears

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:27.060
You act tough and don't listen to anyone

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:32.660
You do this over and over

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:38.400
I shouted until my soul would break

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:43.810
Hurry up and throw that away

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:51.320
We're only heading towards tomorrow

00:22:51.750 --> 00:22:57.060
Close to you  If you're 
trying to find yourself

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:02.890
Just keep doing what you ultimately decided

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:08.370
Close to you  Keep what's 
precious in your heart

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:16.470
There's only one shining 
soul that's next to you
